WEBVTT

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.060
DNA computer connection complete. System normal.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.650
We've received a call from the U.S. Air Force.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:09.310
The early warning radar of the U.S. Air Force has detected an unidentified hypersonic aircraft and is aiming for the Japanese Peninsula.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.870
The air-to-air AWACS has accelerated the aircraft.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.870
It entered our country's air defense control zone.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:20.630
The target is on the southern coast of Iwo Jima.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:22.630
The F-15 is scrambling from the landing site.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.760
It is approaching the target.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:25.760
Are you on alert?

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:26.610
Yes, I am.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.360
It's being analyzed.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.000
What's the situation?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.020
Over.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.700
Blue one, target detected by radar.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.720
Confirmed.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:42.700
Over.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:47.380
Control, target is Mars Harrier Gensokyo.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:53.380
Target detected.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.340
High-speed flight, entering the airfield.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.990
Take reverse course immediately.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:09.060
Target is ignoring the warning and judging the airspace.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.300
Roger that.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.300
Roger that.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.880
Target has been identified.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.120
It is not an aircraft.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.160
Requesting permission.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.450
Target has been identified.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.100
Requesting permission.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.100
Target has been identified.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.080
Unlocking safety device.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.720
Target locked on.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:25.510
Unlocking safety device.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.670
I won't change my mind.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.280
Disappeared from radar in the upper part of Asahara island.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.300
Did it hit the target?

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.910
The missile is not hit.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.360
Image analysis from the satellite has been completed.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:41.220
The Godzilla that destroyed Shinagawa last May was not discovered, despite the search by the Self-Defense Force.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:49.780
Currently, Kiryu is in repair, and the Ministry of Defense has confirmed that there is no risk of rampage like Yokohama and Hakkeijima.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.600
We are now at Yokosuka's Maritime Self-Defense Force base...

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:58.680
This F-1 is Japan's first hypersonic fighter that was developed.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:04.440
It's getting old, so I'm waiting for the results.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.280
Look at this thin body.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.920
It's the line from the cockpit to the bathhouse.

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:14.720
Have you ever touched a real one, Yoshioji-chan?

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:15.880
Shun.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.960
Stop calling me an old man.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:22.800
This was the first one I was in charge of maintenance.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.510
I fixed the F-4 and F-15,

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:28.390
but this is the best among the fighters.

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:30.000
What about Kiryu?

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.790
Kiryu?

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:40.030
Yeah, that's a good mecha, too.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:42.000
All right, it's done!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.700
Yay!

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.850
I'm going to show it to Grandpa!

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:50.090
Grandpa, it's done! Look!

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.380
Huh?

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:52.940
Yeah.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.800
Are you guys dreaming?

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.590
No, we're not.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:57.680
Long time no see, Mr. Chuujou.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.960
Hey!

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:03.280
What happened just now?

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:06.010
Mister, who are these people?

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:10.540
Don't worry. They're old friends.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.790
You remembered them, didn't you?

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:16.650
Of course. There's no way I'll forget them.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.950
The Infant Island.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:25.960
It's been 43 years since our clan first met Mr. Jujou.

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:29.000
I'm getting old too.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:29.720
Just now...

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:54.530
I want you to bring Godzilla's bones back to the sea.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:09:00.000
I want you to bring Godzilla's bones back to the sea.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.530
I made a big mistake.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.720
Did you say you made Kiryu by mistake?

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:10.400
My name is Yoshito.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.830
I'm the security guard of Kiryu in the Special Self-Defense Force.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:20.000
You can't touch the souls of the dead.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:27.240
Godzilla's bones will return to the sea, and they will be buried in the flow of time.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.540
But...

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.980
We need Kiryu to defeat Godzilla!

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:37.480
What if Godzilla comes again?

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:42.480
Then Mothra will risk his life to fight.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.660
Mothra destroyed Tokyo 43 years ago!

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.700
Why would he fight for humans?

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:54.070
Please return Godzilla's bones to the sea.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:59.250
Otherwise, Mothra will have to become an enemy of humans.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:04.790
We don't want that.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.240
Of course, you don't.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:47.640
Because of the battle with Godzilla a year ago, Kiryu damaged 37% of the aircraft, and lost his right arm and absolute zero.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:55.760
However, the repair work is going well, and the repair is already complete for the right arm.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:12:00.000
Director, if Godzilla appears again now, can Kiryu go out?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.940
The Absolut Zero has not been repaired yet, right?

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:11.610
Certainly, the Absolut Zero has not been repaired at this stage.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:15.880
However, the Kiryu can be launched.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.550
He's just saying whatever he wants.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:25.070
If we don't finish the final orbit check, it's impossible to launch.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:26.990
Right, Chujo?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:35.070
-What's wrong, Commander? -Oh, it's nothing.

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:42.030
In the battle a year ago, we gave a great deal of damage to Godzilla and destroyed it.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:50.900
Since then, Godzilla has not been found, even in the search activities using surveillance satellites.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:53.460
-May I ask you one thing? -What is it?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:13:00.000
It is said that Godzilla appeared because he was in line with the body of Godzilla, which was assembled in Kiryu.

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:04.830
I'd like you to tell me about the defense department's opinions on that.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:10.520
What were you doing on your vacation?

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:13.760
I was relaxing at my uncle's villa.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.870
Did something happen at that villa?

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:19.010
Why?

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:26.920
It's unusual for you to be doing nothing while you're working.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:35.050
Yes, sir.

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:39.800
He's a new member of Kiryu.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:13.520
What do you think about Mr. Dobashi's statement that the possibility of Godzilla's appearance is low?

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:30.000
In that case, I think we should prioritize the reconstruction of the city that was destroyed by Godzilla over the huge national budget for the restoration of Kiryu.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:36.090
In Shinagawa, we're still in a dead end, and we don't even know when we'll be back to normal.

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:44.240
But the Kiryu will be an effective defense against special creatures other than Godzilla, right?

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:49.240
Given the current situation of Japan, which may be attacked by a huge creature again,

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:54.450
I'd like to ask the Kiryu who will protect our lives to return to normal.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:15:00.000
Of course, we'll have to recover from the disaster.

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:09.620
We have to tell everyone that we met in a different place.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:13.360
It's a picture of an infant.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:19.770
43 years ago, my grandfather participated in a research group as a linguist.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:27.400
That's when I met them.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.640
The monsters...

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.110
Why did you do that?

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:40.990
The reason Mothra attacked Japan was because the bad guys took her away to make money.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:46.720
Mothra just came to help her.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:54.120
This is the emblem of infanticide that means Mothra.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:59.000
The old men who took her back from the hands of the bad guys

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.390
I drew a paper in the runway at the airport.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:08.610
And I managed to call Mossler there.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:18.630
It's a great loss to get rid of these three from the Kiryu Team.

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:23.040
But for the sake of the more effective warfare and warfare research of the Kiryu,

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:29.700
I want you to learn a lot in the United States as the representative of the Kiryu Team for a year.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:36.020
And now I've grown a little bit more, and I'm back in good shape.

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:39.960
That's all.

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:45.400
When are you leaving for the U.S.?

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.160
I have a special flight tomorrow night.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:51.370
Thank you very much.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:56.230
Have fun at times like this.

00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:57.910
Drink.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.660
You're a professional.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:09.550
Drinking?

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.470
Yeah.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:15.080
You were officially appointed as a Kiryu Taisei pilot.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:16.080
That's right.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:19.300
Can you say something congratulatory?

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.480
As a former member of the maintenance team.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:22.470
What's the relationship?

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.970
Azusa Kisaragi.

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:27.280
We were friends when we were in Kuji four years ago.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.330
We were maintenance team members.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:33.020
Nice to meet you.

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:36.270
Did you become a pilot from the maintenance department?

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:41.750
I really wanted to fly in the sky, so I volunteered for the Kiryu team.

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:45.360
What are you drinking in the corner like this?

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:48.140
Kiryu's Holy Operator, Akiba-kun.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:49.820
Former Kuji's Top Gun.

00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:54.620
He might be good as a pilot, but he treats the aircraft poorly.

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:56.310
That's a pity for the engine.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:03.520
What are you doing?

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:44.370
It's a big mistake for humans to make fighting tools out of Godzilla's bones.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:50.900
Did you make it by mistake?

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:09.280
I'm Chujo of the Kiryu Guard Force.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:11.910
You didn't go to the meeting?

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:15.580
No, I got out of it.

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:17.120
I'm sorry.

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:21.370
I'm not very good at that kind of thing.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:24.260
Me too.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:28.100
Did you come to say goodbye to Kiryu?

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:31.460
It's fine.

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:32.760
It's just a normal conversation.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:36.460
But...

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:42.400
It's a shame that Kiryu is leaving Japan.

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:46.670
Godzilla and I haven't made up our minds yet.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:48.810
Maybe...

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:52.150
Kiryu doesn't want to fight anymore.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:57.770
I wonder if the old king will be happy if he doesn't recover as it is.

00:19:57.770 --> 00:19:59.380
That's not true!

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:03.360
Kiryu's restoration will definitely be done by myself!

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:12.200
I'm counting on you, Kiryu.

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:44.670
So you want me to put an end to the Kiryu Project?

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:47.960
I understand that it's a reckless plan.

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.890
It's a request I made with a friend.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.940
It's true that it's reckless, but I don't think it's worth it.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.700
Can't you trust me?

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:07.260
What does it say?

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:14.120
"Life exists only in the time it is predestined."

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:20.030
The fact that they used Godzilla's bones to make Kiryu was the will of God.

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:24.860
Humans have crossed the line that cannot be crossed.

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:30.000
Don't touch the realm of God.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.060
Human beings are making a mistake in creating Godzilla with nuclear bombs.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:38.670
I believe what you're saying.

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:47.440
But we can't entrust our fate to those who once destroyed Tokyo.

00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:52.500
I also think that someday we have to abandon Kiryu.

00:21:52.500 --> 00:22:00.000
However, as long as the threat of Godzilla exists in reality,

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:07.080
I cannot abandon Kiryu, who is the mastermind for this.

00:22:07.080 --> 00:22:13.420
I have a duty to protect the people.

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:18.050
Even if Kiryu's existence causes a new disaster?

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.760
A huge creature's dead body was found on the coast of Kujukuri.

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:40.010
The Special Self-Defense Force Special Operations Team has been dispatched to search and retrieve the dead body.

00:22:40.010 --> 00:22:42.010
Please step back for the sake of your safety.

00:22:42.010 --> 00:22:45.000
We are not authorized to report.

00:22:54.440 --> 00:23:00.000
In real combat, you can't do anything more than this.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.530
What do you mean by "fighting the real creature"?

00:23:02.530 --> 00:23:06.710
We've finally made it this far in the search for the species, and we've finally gained strength.

00:23:06.710 --> 00:23:10.790
It's a creature that hasn't been confirmed for 17 years.

00:23:10.790 --> 00:23:12.460
It's a turtle, isn't it?

00:23:12.460 --> 00:23:15.010
Oh, you know it well.

00:23:15.010 --> 00:23:22.030
The first answer was found by Professor Mia on the Sergio Island 34 years ago.

00:23:22.030 --> 00:23:23.890
It's a huge mutant turtle.

00:23:23.890 --> 00:23:26.940
There was no other way but to name it a little better.

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:28.740
What's the cause?

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:33.900
There's a deep scar on his neck that looks like it was scratched by a giant nail.

00:23:33.900 --> 00:23:36.650
This must be his fatal wound.

00:23:36.650 --> 00:23:40.650
He's probably been attacked by another giant creature.

00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:43.370
Another giant creature?

00:23:43.370 --> 00:23:46.510
Yes.

00:23:46.510 --> 00:23:50.970
For example, Godzilla.

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:59.760
Captain!

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.460
I've got an unidentified object up our port bow.

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:04.010
All ahead, one third.

00:24:04.010 --> 00:24:04.960
Sonar.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:06.940
Confirm, acoustic sprint.

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:08.740
All ahead, one third.

00:24:08.740 --> 00:24:12.750
Aye aye, sir.

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:14.420
The target is approaching rapidly.

00:24:14.420 --> 00:24:15.660
Distance, 280.

00:24:15.660 --> 00:24:16.880
Fall, right, butter.

00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:17.880
All ahead, fall.

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:18.880
Fall, right, butter.

00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:21.630
All ahead, fall.

00:24:21.630 --> 00:24:23.740
Oh, Jesus.

00:24:23.740 --> 00:24:24.770
Big heartbeats.

00:24:56.430 --> 00:25:00.000
I've told you over and over again.

00:25:00.090 --> 00:25:04.130
As long as we can get the hybrid crystal, we'll be able to repair it immediately.

00:25:04.130 --> 00:25:06.080
There's a limit to our support budget.

00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:09.080
It's impossible to prepare such a huge diamond right away.

00:25:09.080 --> 00:25:11.220
Then we have no choice but to give up.

00:25:11.220 --> 00:25:13.220
Is there anything we can do?

00:25:13.220 --> 00:25:18.270
The hybrid crystal is the heart of Ab-Zero.

00:25:18.270 --> 00:25:20.830
We can't make a diamond so easily.

00:25:20.830 --> 00:25:23.830
Yesterday, an American nuclear submarine left Guam.

00:25:23.830 --> 00:25:27.410
A Godzilla?

00:25:27.410 --> 00:25:30.000
Currently, the location and location are not confirmed.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:33.410
It's under attack. It's a matter of time before we can find it.

00:25:33.410 --> 00:25:36.370
That's why we need to finish the repair as soon as possible.

00:25:37.270 --> 00:25:43.980
Even without the Absolute Zero, the Kiryu will still move.

00:25:43.980 --> 00:25:48.680
I heard that we can launch it.

00:25:48.680 --> 00:25:50.770
We can launch it.

00:25:50.770 --> 00:25:54.030
Please wait! The final adjustments for each unit are not finished yet!

00:25:54.030 --> 00:25:55.950
We can't launch it!

00:25:55.950 --> 00:25:59.700
Captain, just like he said, it's not in its complete state yet.

00:26:00.480 --> 00:26:06.410
We can go out, but if we keep fighting and get further damage...

00:26:06.410 --> 00:26:10.170
Kiryu might never be able to recover.

00:26:10.170 --> 00:26:14.630
How long will it take until the final adjustment is complete?

00:26:14.630 --> 00:26:17.180
At least half a month.

00:26:17.180 --> 00:26:19.500
I can't wait that long.

00:26:19.500 --> 00:26:24.680
What are you going to do if Godzilla appears in the meantime?

00:26:31.210 --> 00:26:35.560
You really don't want Kiryu to go out?

00:26:35.560 --> 00:26:39.860
Your uncle went to visit Prime Minister Igarashi, didn't he?

00:26:39.860 --> 00:26:44.740
He told him to cancel the Kiryu Project.

00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:50.540
If you abandon Kiryu, Mothra will protect Japan.

00:26:50.540 --> 00:26:55.660
Are you scared of fighting Godzilla?

00:26:55.660 --> 00:26:57.410
Stop it, Chujo!

00:26:57.410 --> 00:26:59.570
What do you know, Uren?

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.860
I've been taking care of Kiri all this time!

00:27:01.860 --> 00:27:03.860
You know Kiri a little bit better than I do!

00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:09.700
You're a professional in defense.

00:27:09.700 --> 00:27:11.940
I'm a professional who fights on the front lines.

00:27:11.940 --> 00:27:30.000
It's important.

00:27:30.120 --> 00:27:37.150
I understand how you feel, but it's been like that for a long time.

00:27:37.150 --> 00:27:42.630
The engine is crying, the high-power equipment is in danger.

00:27:42.630 --> 00:27:46.360
The Vulcan cannon is laughing.

00:27:46.360 --> 00:27:49.150
Mecha has too much love for you.

00:27:49.150 --> 00:27:53.650
I didn't say the Vulcan cannon was laughing.

00:27:53.650 --> 00:27:58.580
I understand how you feel, but I don't understand how humans feel.

00:28:01.600 --> 00:28:02.940
You fought with Akiba, didn't you?

00:28:04.070 --> 00:28:05.560
I'm sorry.

00:28:05.680 --> 00:28:06.630
Forget about the fight.

00:28:07.210 --> 00:28:08.960
Did you do something bad?

00:28:09.760 --> 00:28:11.650
